From: Lukas Klizas <lukas@klizas.lt>
Subject: [PATCH] hwmon: macsmc-hwmon: set platform drvdata; fix NULL deref on resume

macsmc_hwmon_probe() never calls platform_set_drvdata(). The hwmon
pointer is only passed to devm_hwmon_device_register_with_info(),
which stores it as drvdata of the hwmon class device, not of the
platform device.

macsmc_hwmon_resume() reads dev_get_drvdata(&pdev->dev) -- always
NULL -- and dereferences hwmon->smc: NULL pointer dereference at
0x8 inside dpm_resume(), killing systemd-sleep while user.slice is
still frozen. Net effect on a T2 MacBookPro16,1: hard freeze on
every S3 resume once the driver binds (the is_acpi Intel-Mac
binding is new in the cachyos-7.1.3-1 tree; DT-only builds never
bound on these machines, hiding the bug).

Oops fingerprint: RIP macsmc_hwmon_resume+0x2b, CR2=0x8,
r13 (drvdata) = 0, Comm systemd-sleep, via platform_pm_resume ->
dpm_run_callback.

Set the platform drvdata in probe.

Signed-off-by: Lukas Klizas <lukas@klizas.lt>
---
 drivers/hwmon/macsmc-hwmon.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/hwmon/macsmc-hwmon.c
+++ b/drivers/hwmon/macsmc-hwmon.c
@@ -1359,6 +1359,8 @@
 		return dev_err_probe(hwmon->dev, PTR_ERR(hwmon->hwmon_dev),
 				     "Probing SMC hwmon device failed\n");
 
+	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, hwmon);
+
 	dev_dbg(hwmon->dev, "Registered SMC hwmon device. Sensors:\n");
 	dev_dbg(hwmon->dev,
 		"Current: %d, Fans: %d, Power: %d, Temperature: %d, Voltage: %d",
